       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, with a maximum of about 1,000 mg in a single dose. The order is about twice the daily maximum.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a transposition or a total-daily-dose mix-up. Possible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO with meals, at a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is deliberate, please confirm that. I'd also add a note documenting the rationale."
