       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. The dose is 5,100 mg/day, twice the labeled maximum. Each 1,700 mg dose is also well above the single-dose range. I know of no indication that supports it, and the main harm is lactic acidosis, which can be severe or fatal.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Metformin 1,700 mg/day total, split as 850 mg PO twice daily\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, please discuss it with pharmacy first. The order would then need to go through your institution's dose-override process, not through me."
